---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const title = "Payload Yaw Control";
const description =
  "Development of a payload yaw control system using reinforcement learning, image-based pose estimation, and Raspberry Pi.";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.ico`} />

    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <nav class="project-nav">
    <!--  <a href="#part02">Part 2</a> -->
      <a href={`${base}/en/overview`}>Part 1</a>
      Part 2
      <a href={`${base}/en/contact`}>Contact</a>
      <a href={`${base}/ja/`}>日本語</a>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="hero-subtitle">
          Demonstration using Reinforcement Learning,
          Image-based Pose Estimation,
          and Raspberry Pi
        </p>

        <h1>Payload Yaw Control</h1>

        <p class="hero-text">
          This project develops an autonomous payload yaw control system<br />
          by combining image-based pose estimation with reinforcement learning.
          <br />
          The estimated yaw angle is used to control four thrusters
          in real time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="part-links">
        <article>
          <p class="part-label">Part 2 — Latest</p>

          <h2>Low-Power Variable Target Yaw Control</h2>

          <p>
            A single control model supports target yaw angles of
            0°, ±45°, and ±90°.
            Low-power control is evaluated using three payload types.
          </p>

          <a href="#part02">Overview</a>
          <!--<a href={`${base}en/part02/`}>Read Part 2</a>-->
        </article>

        <article>
          <p class="part-label">Part 1</p>

          <h2>Image-based Payload Yaw Control</h2>

          <p>
            A baseline system that estimates payload yaw from camera images
            and executes the learned controller in real time on Raspberry Pi.
          </p>

          <a href="#part01">Overview</a>
          <a href={`${base}en/overview`}>Read Part 1</a>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section id="part02" class="part-summary">
        <h2>Part 2 Overview</h2>

        <p>
          Part 2 extends the baseline system by introducing variable target yaw
          control and low-power thruster control.
          The controller is evaluated for three payload types at
          0°, ±45°, and ±90°.
        </p>
        <video controls muted playsinline preload="metadata">
          <source
            src={`${base}videos/Part02/HSteel_0001-1900.mp4`}
            type="video/mp4"
          />
        </video>        
      </section>

      <section id="part01" class="part-summary">
        <h2>Part 1 Overview</h2>

        <p>
          Part 1 presents the baseline payload yaw control system combining
          image-based yaw estimation, reinforcement learning,
          and real-time execution on Raspberry Pi.
        </p>

        <video controls muted playsinline preload="metadata">
          <source
            src={`${base}videos/With_Without_Control-Raspberry_Pi.mp4`}
            type="video/mp4"
          />
        </video>

        <p class="hero-caption">
          This demonstration shows real-time payload yaw control on Raspberry Pi
          using yaw angles estimated from camera images.
          The left shows the proposed control system, while the right shows the
          same conditions without control.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer lang="en" />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .project-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
  }

  main {
    width: min(100% - 40px, 960px);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero {
    padding: 80px 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-subtitle,
  .part-label {
    color: #666;
  }

  .hero-text {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .part-links {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .part-links article {
    padding: 24px;
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
  }

  .part-links a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 12px 18px 0 0;
  }

  .part-summary {
    padding: 72px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  video {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .hero-caption {
    width: min(100%, 760px);
    margin: 12px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #555;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .part-links {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>